   Ciencia \& Technol},
Abstract = {This paper describes the results obtained for the production and
   characterization of a radioactive C-11 beam, by means of the in flight
   technique at the tandem laboratory of the National Institute of Nuclear
   Research, Mexico. The C-11 production technique described here, uses the
   well known Associated Particle Technique (APT) with the reaction
   H-2(B-10,C-11)n, in order to obtain a biunivocal correspondence between
   the radioactive C-11 particles and the associated neutrons. A discussion
   concerning the possible use of this C-11 beam in the study of the
   elastic scattering of protons is introduced.},
