   BRAZIL, AUG 03-07, 2009},
Organization = {Int Astron Union; Observ Nacl; IAU Div II, III \& IV},
Abstract = {We analyze Si iv 139.37 um emission line during solar Explosive Events
   (EE) near the center of the solar disk with the aim to study the
   structure of the sources of EEs observed at the VUV. The observations
   were made by SUMER, on board SoHO, with a raster regime of six EW
   positions that allowed us to identify the times and EW, NS positions of
   the maximum amplitude of each EE. Based on one dimensional NS
   distributions at three different wavelengths (blue, central and red) for
   times around each maximum we have identified three different shapes of
   the sources. Also. It was found that the maximum at the blue wing is
   attained after the maxima, at red and central wavelengths.},
