   jeconia ombra Evans, 1955 from eastern Ecuador. Chusquea scandens
   (Poaceae, Bambusoidea) is the larval food plant. Larvae in all stadia
   build shelters and forcibly eject frass with the aid of an anal comb.
   Later instars possess an eversible prothoracic ``neck{''} gland. Larvae
   are associated with moving water.},
