   how does the decomposition of a polynomial P as the product of
   polynomials behave under perturbations of P? How do the eigenvalues,
   eigenspaces and more generally invariant subspaces of an operator A
   behave under perturbations of A? We give a characterization of the
   regular situations and describe completely the singular ones in some
   moderately degenerate situations.},
